WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
Who decides?

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:04.214
The book's advice: name the
people allowed to say no,

3
00:00:04.214 --> 00:00:09.038
give each decision one of them, and make
the repository remember who said yes.

4
00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:12.312
The book uses Book 01's
program-wide model.

5
00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:17.067
The executive sponsor, with the CIO,
owns scope, funding and sequence,

6
00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:21.737
breaks ties, and decides when
Active Directory components retire.

7
00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:26.257
The CISO sets the control requirements
every target surface must meet:

8
00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:30.550
authentication strength, the
Conditional Access baseline, logging.

9
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.481
The authorizing official
is the only official

10
00:00:33.481 --> 00:00:36.037
who can accept security and privacy risk.

11
00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:39.597
The steward leads the program
office and owns the plan,

12
00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:43.788
wave sequencing, cross-domain
dependencies and the repository.

13
00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:48.420
A change to the target architecture, or
to the rules for authoritative origin,

14
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.025
needs the steward and
the sponsor together.

15
00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:54.563
HR decides what each
organizational attribute means.

16
00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:59.374
And workstream leads own their designs,
inside the CISO's requirements.

17
00:00:59.374 --> 00:01:03.650
Two federal requirements already name
people who belong in these rows.

18
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:09.085
M-22-09 required a zero trust
implementation lead within 30 days,

19
00:01:09.085 --> 00:01:10.613
and an aligned C-suite.

20
00:01:10.613 --> 00:01:16.537
M-19-17 requires an integrated,
agency-wide ICAM governance structure.

21
00:01:16.537 --> 00:01:20.838
So the decision for the sponsor and
CIO, in Phase 0: name the sponsor,

22
00:01:20.838 --> 00:01:23.467
the steward and the steering committee,

23
00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:27.500
and build them from those existing
roles, not alongside them.
